Input: {"question": "When was the Sumter County Courthouse built?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d00", "start": 0, "end": 143, "text": "Sumter County Courthouse (Alabama) The Sumter County Courthouse is a historic county courthouse building in Livingston, Sumter County, Alabama."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d00", "start": 144, "end": 253, "text": "Designed in the Beaux-Arts style, it has served as the Sumter County Courthouse since its completion in 1902."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d00", "start": 254, "end": 370, "text": "The two-story structure is built of red brick, with terracotta architectural elements, over a stone clad foundation."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d00", "start": 371, "end": 405, "text": "It is topped by a dome and cupola."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d00", "start": 406, "end": 455, "text": "It was designed by Chapman and Frederick Ausfeld."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d00", "start": 456, "end": 559, "text": "The Sumter County Courthouse is centered in a large town square, that is enclosed within an iron fence."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d00", "start": 560, "end": 623, "text": "An adjacent bored well pavilion, built in brick in 1924; and an"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d01", "start": 0, "end": 241, "text": "showing the location of Sumter County Courthouse Location US 11 , Livingston , Alabama Coordinates 32°34′58″N 88°11′18″W ﻿ / ﻿ 32.58278°N 88.18833°W ﻿ / 32.58278 ; -88.18833 Area 2 acres ( 0.81 ha ) Built 1902 ( 1902 ) Built by Dabbs , C.H ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d01", "start": 242, "end": 248, "text": "& Co ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d01", "start": 249, "end": 337, "text": "Architect Frederick Ausfeld & Chapman Architectural style Beaux Arts NRHP reference No ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d01", "start": 338, "end": 494, "text": "72000180 [ 1 ] Added to NRHP March 24 , 1972 The Sumter County Courthouse is a historic county courthouse building in Livingston , Sumter County , Alabama ."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d01", "start": 495, "end": 537, "text": "[ 1 ] Description [ edit ] Designed in the"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d02", "start": 0, "end": 47, "text": "a Revolutionary War hero who served in the U.S."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d02", "start": 48, "end": 55, "text": "Senate."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d02", "start": 56, "end": 138, "text": "The first courthouse was a log structure in 1833 and served the county until 1837."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d02", "start": 139, "end": 216, "text": "In 1838, a second courthouse was constructed but collapsed and was torn down."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d02", "start": 217, "end": 277, "text": "Sumter became the center of antebellum civilization in 1840."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d02", "start": 278, "end": 373, "text": "A third courthouse was constructed in 1855 and served until 1901 when it was destroyed by fire."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d02", "start": 374, "end": 475, "text": "Its cornerstone was laid in 1902, and the two-story brick and stone building still serves the county."}, "D3S8": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d02", "start": 476, "end": 538, "text": "It was added to the National Register 