": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d03", "start": 479, "end": 482, "text": "[1]"}, "D4S15": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d03", "start": 484, "end": 502, "text": "Description [edit]"}, "D4S16": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d03", "start": 503, "end": 640, "text": "Designed in the Beaux Arts style, the Sumter County Courthouse stands as a testament to the architectural trends of the mid-19th century."}, "D4S17": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d03", "start": 641, "end": 672, "text": "Constructed in 1850 by the firm"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d04", "start": 0, "end": 149, "text": "Sumter County Courthouse (Florida) The Sumter County Courthouse, built in 1912-1914, is an historic courthouse building located in Bushnell, Florida."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d04", "start": 150, "end": 214, "text": "The total costs of construction for the courthouse were $56,000."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d04", "start": 215, "end": 459, "text": "It was designed by Atlanta-based architect William Augustus Edwards who designed one other courthouse in Florida, two in Georgia and nine in South Carolina as well as academic buildings at 12 institutions in Florida, Georgia and South Carolina."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d04", "start": 460, "end": 561, "text": "He designed most of the original buildings on the campus of the University of Florida in Gainesville."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d04", "start": 562, "end": 659, "text": "In 1989, The Sumter County Courthouse was listed in \"A Guide to Florida's Historic Architecture\","}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d05", "start": 0, "end": 99, "text": "Carolina as well as academic buildings at 12 institutions in Florida , Georgia and South Carolina ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d05", "start": 100, "end": 202, "text": "He designed most of the original buildings on the campus of the University of Florida in Gainesville ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d05", "start": 203, "end": 354, "text": "[ 2 ] In 1989 , The Sumter County Courthouse was listed in A Guide to Florida 's Historic Architecture , published by the University of Florida Press ."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d05", "start": 355, "end": 572, "text": "[ 3 ] There is now a much larger Sumter County Judicial Building nearby which bears a striking resemblance to the 1912-1914 courthouse because it incorporates much of its architectural features in its central facade ."}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d06", "start": 0, "end": 201, "text": "Sumter County Courthouse (South Carolina) The Sumter County Courthouse, built in 1907, is an historic courthouse located at 141 North Main Street in the city of Sumter in Sumter County, South Carolina."}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d06", "start": 202, "end": 428, "text": "It was designed in the Beaux Arts style by Darlington native William Augustus Edwards who designed eight other South Carolina courthouses as well as academic buildings at 12 institutions in Florida, Georgia and South Carolina."}, "D7S3": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d06", "start": 429, "end": 456, "text": "It was built in an I-shape."}, "D7S4": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d06", "start": 457, "end": 506, "text": "In the early 1960s it was enlarged and remodeled."}, "D7S5": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0475-da15e0fe83c9:d06", "start": 507, "end": 582, "text": "On June 16, 2004, it was added to the National Register of Historic Places."}, "D7S6": {"docum